ose who have need?<br /> <br /> Who are those eight Uratha, I wonder?</div> </div> </div> </div>We do not speak of the ninth, its senses filled with a bright bloody star of lifelong fraternal torment since its distant childhood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T12:02:06-08:00","id":339262,"title":"","content":"From what I've read, The vikings used to have cults worshiping wolf spirits who would reward their worshipers around this time of year.<br /> <br /> And according to legend, those born on Christmas would be cursed to become werewolves by god because he was mad that a mortal had the gall to be born on the same day as his son.<br /> <br /> And the wild chirstmas parties that the hounds of god would hold after their battles in Baltic legends... Actually there are a lot of Christmas related werewolf legends now that I think of it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T13:15:56-08:00","id":339369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/339173-happy-wolfidays-to-all?p=339262#post339262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've read, The vikings used to have cults worshiping wolf spirits who would reward their worshipers around this time of year.<br /> <br /> And according to legend, those born on Christmas would be cursed to become werewolves by god because he was mad that a mortal had the gall to be born on the same day as his son.<br /> <br /> And the wild chirstmas parties that the hounds of god would hold after their battles in Baltic legends... Actually there are a lot of Christmas related werewolf legends now that I think of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We need a picture of an Uratha wrapped up in tinsel and wrapping material with a lil' bow on top. In wolfy form, of course.<br /> <br /> &quot;I can haz Kibble 'n' Magath now??&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div alig